Z||000000||BlackARROW||10-02-2001||07:56 PM||||Arriving at my place tonight, it stalled. I restarted it, when to park it, and it stalled again.  Allright, it is steady now, but it would start up again.<P><BR>What I know:<P><BR>- new spark plugs<BR>- new wires<BR>- new distributor<BR>- new fuel filter<BR>- new batterie<BR>- 3/4 Gas Tank<P><BR>During the last 2 days, I've been experiencing power lost, and some lifters clicking like I'm used too. I've been hearing something in the back recently too - something vacuuming or tight induction on quick acceleration.  Since I have installed my K filter (a week ago), I've been having some good time ridding it; not much more than 4000rpm (never in the red).  So I think (and hope) it is not related to that.<P>I've had blue smoke coming out of the exhaust at start up, if that can help you help me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'll try to start it again a little bit later, to see if it will work once cooled down. <P><BR>Suggestions for troubleshooting would be of a great help?<P><BR>I've got a Fiero 4cyl, '85.<P><BR>Thanks a lot<P><BR>BlackARROW<BR>..it sucks when it does that..<P><BR>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"<p>[This message has been edited by BlackARROW (edited 10-02-2001).]||||reg||8
